WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.720
This is a right angled triangle.
One leg is 3, the other is 4.

2
00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:10.090
The short leg is 3 units long.

3
00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:13.320
The long leg is 4 units long.

4
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.650
Let's make a square on the short leg:
3 × 3 = 9 tiles.

5
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.120
Let's make another square on the long leg:
4 × 4 = 16 tiles.

6
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:37.350
Do 9 and 16 tiles fill a square
on the hypotenuse, the slanted side?

7
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.550
Watch them move.

8
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.050
3 squared plus 4 squared …

9
00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:50.250
… is 9 + 16 tiles.

10
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.400
25 tiles fill it exactly.

11
00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:02.720
And 25 is 5 squared:
the 5-by-5 square on the hypotenuse.

12
00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:08.170
In every right triangle:
a squared, plus b squared equals c²

13
00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:12.750
a and b are the 2 legs;
and c is the hypotenuse.

14
00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:17.400
Does it hold for other so called Pythagorean triples?

15
00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:21.620
The square on the 5 side:
25 tiles.

16
00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:25.920
On the 12 side: 144 tiles.

17
00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:29.470
Do they fill the square
on the hypotenuse?

18
00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:37.670
Exactly: 169 tiles.
5-squared, plus 12-squared equals 13-squared.

19
00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:42.890
One more Pythagorean triple: 8, 15, 17.

20
00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:47.170
The square on the 8 side:
64 tiles.

21
00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:51.500
On the 15 side: 225 tiles.

22
00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:53.830
Do they fit again?

23
00:01:55.100 --> 00:02:03.100
Exactly: 289 tiles.
8 squared, plus 15 squared equals 17 squared.

24
00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:06.700
Made with Strata.
